summary:
Implement the single combined AlembicAgent landing for the confirmed Recipe production/retrieval-quality demand, consuming accepted AlembicCore commit b711ea10aa5c67d1d75a58a18c0d56623e26c290 through its public contracts.

Required connected implementation:
1. Inventory the real Agent Recipe-producing call graph, including knowledge.submit, session-bound/opportunistic variants, and any cold-start or incremental producer path actually owned by Agent. Preserve non-Recipe behavior, but every Recipe submit must terminate at Core RecipeProductionPort with capability=knowledge-submit (or the exact other one of the four confirmed capabilities only where a real Agent caller owns it); do not call KnowledgeService.create or rebuild Core readiness/profile semantics locally.
2. Extend Agent producer schemas, prompts and deterministic front-loading so equivalent source evidence produces the Core RecipeRetrievalProfile semantics: project-primary summary, evidence-grounded technical English summary/concepts/scenarios/exclusions, stable provenance/source refs and source-content hash. English text is retrieval expression only; never use frozen queries, expected Recipe IDs, hardcoded/global synonyms, provider/rank output or invented facts.
3. Remove or replace unsafe mechanical coreCode repair. coreCode may be emitted only from a cited bounded code range matching the evidence; an invalid, unbounded, whole-file or unrelated-document range must leave coreCode empty or produce a stable Core readiness violation while the candidate remains pending/staging. Do not make provider/vector availability a submit or publish gate.
4. Surface Core readiness/profile violations in the existing Agent result/stop-loss evidence without parsing prose, preserve evidence ledger and session behavior, and keep pending/staging repairable truth. Do not add a second profile database/status machine or bypass publish readiness.
5. Keep changes confined to AlembicAgent; no Plugin/Alembic/Dashboard/Core edits, no real knowledge-root writes, no query ranking/Graph/Test work.

Required RED/GREEN and exit evidence:
- schema-to-runtime validation parity for every real Agent Recipe submit variant;
- equivalent evidence across cold/opportunistic/session-bound submit variants yields the same profile semantics where those variants exist;
- bounded range produces matching coreCode/provenance; whole-file, invalid and unrelated ranges cannot inject code and cannot activate;
- missing/ungrounded profile facts remain pending/staging with stable Core violation codes;
- provider offline does not change deterministic readiness or Agent submit result truth;
- real in-test Agent call reaches Core RecipeProductionPort and persists/profile-projects through the accepted contract; no empty adapter or disconnected type-only work;
- focused and full Agent tests, build/type/lint/import-boundary gates, git diff/check, two-stage self-review, clean single AlembicAgent commit with exact parent/commit and residual risks.
